@title Product Design Principles
@subtitle Fathom Bank Design Systems, for every design review
@author Design Systems team

These principles were agreed in a workshop with 26 designers and engineers on 2026-09-17. They apply to all customer-facing apps, and every design review should check work against them.

# Clarity over cleverness

Customers come to us to get something done, not to admire the interface. When a clever pattern and a plain one both work, choose the plain one, especially where money moves.

- **Do**: label buttons with the action they take.
- **Avoid**: icons without text for money movement.

# Show the money

Fees, rates and totals are the part of any screen customers care about most. Show them early and plainly, so that nobody reaches the end of a flow surprised by a number.

- **Do**: show fees before confirmation.
- **Avoid**: revealing fees on the final screen.

# Forgive mistakes

Everyone taps the wrong thing sometimes. A good flow makes mistakes cheap to undo, so customers can act with confidence instead of fear.

- **Do**: allow undo for 10 seconds after a transfer is scheduled.
- **Avoid**: making cancellation a phone call.

# Accessible by default

Accessibility is part of the design from the start, not a fix added at the end. If a design does not work for every customer, it is not finished.

- **Do**: meet a contrast ratio of 4.5 to 1.
- **Avoid**: relying on color alone for status.

# Calm, not urgent

Financial decisions deserve time. We give customers the facts they need and let them decide at their own pace, without manufactured pressure.

- **Do**: state plain deadlines.
- **Avoid**: countdown timers that push decisions.

---

> If a customer has to read it twice, we wrote it wrong.
> — Ines Albrecht, Head of Design

! Disagreements with a principle go to the monthly design council, not to individual reviews.
